comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T04:54:11.196Z",codex-sol,"Refreshed read-only inventory is in docs/release-migration.md: 34 package copies at recorded checkout heads, including pm-memory. Remaining migration prerequisites include the missing pm-context release:notes script, preserved approval/manual-only guards, package-specific workflow-shape tests, pm-vcs binary bundle disposition and representative Rust/Postgres callers. The release-continuation implementation only pilots pm-ops; live trusted-publisher/event acceptance, account-wide admission fixtures and the post-window measurements remain with the fleet rollout owner."
  "2026-11-06T07:24:55.482Z",codex-agent,"Additional rollout evidence: canonical tags through v2026.10.19 predate daily-release.yml, so the legacy checker compatibility exception certifies the tag pin, not existence of a reusable workflow at those old commits. The migration docs already require checking workflow existence at the selected released SHA. Preserve that prerequisite in the wave tooling; a later checker enhancement can add explicit missing-workflow refusal without conflating it with this review round permission fix."
